; g7x-probe.ngc -- a G72 facing cycle and a G71 turning cycle, for comparing
; LiNC's preview against what the controller really cuts.
;
; Every coordinate is a literal. There is no loop and no #<_x>/#<_z> anywhere,
; so both pictures should agree: anything they disagree on is the cycle's own
; geometry (where it puts its passes, how deep, how far apart), not the
; preview's expression evaluation.
;
; Part 1 faces a stepped profile at Z-10..-2. Part 2 turns the same shape 20
; further out in Z. They sit apart so the two cycles cannot be confused.

G21 G54 G18 G90 G8
F400
G0 X0 Z2
m3 s1000

; ---- part 1: G72 facing -------------------------------------------------
; Profile, in the order the cycle reads it: (X0 Z-10), (X4 Z-10), (X4 Z-6),
; (X8 Z-6), (X8 Z-2). X never decreases, which G72 requires.
; The cycle's X1 Z1 replace the profile's first point, so part 1 starts at
; (X1 Z1) and the face it steps back from is Z1.
O100 SUB
G0 X0 Z-10
G1 X4 Z-10
G1 X4 Z-6
G1 X8 Z-6
G1 X8 Z-2
O100 ENDSUB

G72 Q100 X1 Z1 D0.5 I1 R0.3
G70 Q100 X1 Z1 D0.5 P1

; ---- part 2: G71 turning ------------------------------------------------
; Same shape, 20 further out. Z never decreases, which G71 requires.
; X10 starts above the profile, so the layers step inward.
O101 SUB
G0 X0 Z10
G1 X4 Z10
G1 X4 Z14
G1 X8 Z14
G1 X8 Z18
O101 ENDSUB

G71 Q101 X10 Z9 D0.5 I1 R0.3
G70 Q101 X10 Z9 D0.5 P1

G0 X0 Z30
M2
